# EAS Build upload rules.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS — do not delete it.
#
# EAS CLI uploads the project by cloning with `--no-checkout` and then copying
# the working directory through a gitignore filter. Because the clone carries no
# checked-out files and the copy step matches patterns only (it never consults
# git's index), any file matching .gitignore is dropped — *even if it is tracked*.
#
# .env matches .gitignore, so it never reached the EAS builder. Every standalone
# Android build therefore bundled an empty Supabase URL and died on launch with
# `supabaseUrl is required.` — while development worked, because `expo start`
# reads .env straight from disk.
#
# When .easignore exists, EAS ignores .gitignore entirely and uses only the rules
# below. .env is deliberately NOT excluded here, which is what makes it upload.
#
# IMPORTANT: because this file replaces .gitignore for uploads, any new
# .gitignore entry must be mirrored here or it will be shipped to the builder.

node_modules
.expo

# Editor / OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.log

# Never upload local native projects — EAS regenerates them from app config.
android
ios
